<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-GRIQUAS REQUIRE 302 FOR VICTORY VS BORDER.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-GRIQUAS REQUIRE 302 FOR VICTORY VS BORDER.</headline>
<dateline>EAST LONDON 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Griqualand West face the</p>
<p>mammoth task of scoring 302 runs on a deteriorating pitch on the</p>
<p>final day of their Supersport series match against Border at</p>
<p>Buffalo Park on Monday. </p>
<p>At the close on Sunday Griquas had already lost opener</p>
<p>Martyn Gidley for 11 and were 38 for one.</p>
<p>Griquas had resumed their innings in the morning on 177 for</p>
<p>five but were all out just before lunch for 253 with Piet</p>
<p>Barnard's 79 the top score.</p>
<p>Border opener Piet Botha was the mainstay of the home side's</p>
<p>second innngs scoring 90 not out with nine fours as they</p>
<p>declared their innings closed at 192 for five -- a lead of 339.</p>
